	<!-- Seasons of the Zone - everything the mod says in game: the PDA app's two pages,
	     its PDA messages, and the transmissions on the days the Zone marks. The MCM pages
	     are in ui_seasons_of_the_zone.xml.

	     A translation copies this file and ui_seasons_of_the_zone.xml to
	     configs/text/<language>/ and translates each <text>, keeping every id; a text not
	     translated yet can stay English. The encoding stays windows-1251.

	     $name is a value the game fills in: a place, a count, a date, a season. Put it
	     wherever the sentence needs it, and keep its name as it is.

	     $Season and $season are the same season: $Season as it starts a line or a
	     sentence ("Deep winter"), $season inside one ("deep winter"). $From and $from,
	     $To and $to, $Next and $next, $Pinned and $pinned work the same way. A season
	     the player named in configure.bat has one form, which fills both.

	     An id written as <id>_one and <id>_many takes a count, $n, and the game picks the
	     form by the rule st_sotz_plural_rule names. "en": _one for 1, _many for the rest.
	     "ru": _one for 1, 21, 31..., _few for 2-4, 22-24..., _many for the rest, so a
	     Russian table adds an <id>_few beside each pair. A missing form falls back to
	     _many.

	     Keep each text on one line, with no run of spaces and none at either end: X-Ray
	     reads these files with TinyXML, which by default collapses them. -->

	<string id="st_sotz_plural_rule"><text>en</text></string>

